From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kernel32/tests: the rasapi32 api set load fails as on Windows

kernel32/tests: module.c checks that LoadLibraryEx of the rasapi32 api set
with LOAD_LIBRARY_SEARCH_APPLICATION_DIR fails; it was todo_wine because
Wine's rasapi32 had no dependencies outside the system directory. Ours now
has (the RAS patches of this integration), the check passes as on Windows
and "succeeded inside todo" was a new conformance failure. Found by the
stage D comparison.
---
diff --git a/dlls/kernel32/tests/module.c b/dlls/kernel32/tests/module.c
--- a/dlls/kernel32/tests/module.c
+++ b/dlls/kernel32/tests/module.c
@@ -803,7 +803,8 @@ static void test_LoadLibraryEx_search_flags(void)
         ok( GetLastError() == ERROR_MOD_NOT_FOUND, "wrong error %lu\n", GetLastError() );
         SetLastError( 0xdeadbeef );
         mod = LoadLibraryExA( "ext-ms-win-ras-rasapi32-l1-1-0.dll", NULL, LOAD_LIBRARY_SEARCH_APPLICATION_DIR );
-        todo_wine /* rasapi32 doesn't have interesting dependencies on wine */
+        /* Stained Glass OS: our rasapi32 imports what Windows' does (not found in the
+         * application directory), so this fails as on Windows: no todo */
         ok( !mod, "rasapi32 loaded\n" );
         if (mod) FreeLibrary( mod );
         else ok( GetLastError() == ERROR_MOD_NOT_FOUND, "wrong error %lu\n", GetLastError() );
